# Surgical line-ending pins for a game mod: only the text surfaces whose
# own tooling cares about line endings are normalised, leaving data and
# binary assets to git's own detection. bash and shellcheck reject CRLF,
# so every shell surface
# must be LF on disk - the run-lint / fix-permissions shims under
# scripts/, Gradle's gradlew launcher, and any composite-action scripts
# under .github/. A stray CR on a shebang line otherwise yields
#   env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# on a Linux CI runner.
*.sh    text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# yamllint's new-lines rule reports CRLF as an error. A Linux CI runner
# checks these out as LF whatever the repository holds, so without a pin
# the rule passes in CI and fails on a Windows working copy - the same
# command disagreeing with itself by platform. Pinned so the local run
# and the gate see one file.
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# cmd.exe requires CRLF in batch files.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
